      "node_id": "kg_doc_7",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Robert Erskine Childers DSC (25 June 1870 – 24 November 1922), universally known as Erskine Childers, was a British writer, whose works included the influential novel \"The Riddle of the Sands\", and a Fenian revolutionary who smuggled guns to Ireland in his sailing yacht \"Asgard\". He was executed by the authorities of the nascent Irish Free State during the Irish Civil War. He was the son of British Orientalist scholar Robert Caesar Childers; the cousin of Hugh Childers and Robert Barton; and the father of the fourth President of Ireland, Erskine Hamilton Childers.",
